      answer: 0,
      why: 'Bragg\'s law: nλ = 2d·sinθ, so sinθ = 0.154/(2 × 0.308) = 0.25, θ ≈ 14.5°. The reflected beam emerges at 29° from the incident direction — the factor of 2 in the law is the classic exam trap and the physical heart of the method.',
